# ATS Web UI Standards

- Build mobile-first layouts, then scale for tablet and desktop breakpoints.
- Use reusable UI primitives and consistent spacing/type tokens.
- Keep pages composition-focused; move logic into hooks and services.
- Prefer server components; use client components only where interactivity is needed.

# Professional UX Baseline

- Every main screen must include loading, empty, error, and success states.
- Use accessible labels, keyboard navigation, and WCAG-compliant contrast.
- Keep tables performant with pagination, filtering, and debounced search.
- Candidate pipeline drag/drop must support keyboard fallback actions.

# Visual Consistency

- Use one design language: card sections, sticky page actions, clear hierarchy.
- Keep micro-interactions subtle (hover/focus/active), avoid noisy animations.
- Use avatar/status chips/tags consistently across candidate, job, and interview views.

# Example

```tsx
<PageShell title="Candidates" subtitle="Track pipeline across all jobs">
  <CandidateFilters />
  <CandidateTable />
</PageShell>
```
